# NFA Pipeline 🎬

A production-grade Python data pipeline for scraping, transforming, validating, and storing data from the **National Film Awards (NFA)** website hosted by the Directorate of Film Festivals (DFF), Government of India.

---

## Features

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| **Extraction** | Multi-strategy HTML parser (tables → definition lists → heading heuristics) |
| **Transformation** | Unicode normalisation, language aliasing, award-type inference, title casing |
| **Validation** | Field-level + cross-field + batch-level checks with configurable thresholds |
| **Storage** | SQLite (queryable), Excel (formatted workbook), CSV |
| **Resumable** | JSON checkpoint — re-run after crash picks up where it left off |
| **Polite scraping** | robots.txt compliance, random delay, exponential-backoff retries |
| **On-disk cache** | TTL-based HTML caching — avoids re-hitting the server unnecessarily |
| **Logging** | Rotating file + colourised console at configurable verbosity |
| **Configuration** | Single YAML file with environment variable override support |
| **CLI** | Full argparse CLI with `--years`, `--dry-run`, `--status`, `--force` |
| **Tests** | pytest test suite with coverage |

---

## Project Structure

```
