## Quick Start

### 1. Install

```bash
# Clone the repo
git clone https://github.com/your-org/nfa-pipeline.git
cd nfa-pipeline

# Create a virtual environment
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate       # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate

# Install with dev dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"
# OR production only:
pip install .
```

### 2. Run the Pipeline

```bash
# Full run — years 2000–2023
python -m nfa_pipeline

# Or using the Makefile shortcut
make run
```

### 3. Check What Would Run (Dry Run)

```bash
python -m nfa_pipeline --dry-run
# DRY RUN — would scrape 24 years: [2000, 2001, ..., 2023]
```

### 4. Run Specific Years

```bash
# Single years
python -m nfa_pipeline --years 2015 2016 2017

# Year range
python -m nfa_pipeline --start-year 2010 --end-year 2015
```

---

## CLI Reference

```
python -m nfa_pipeline [OPTIONS]

Year selection:
  --years YEAR [YEAR ...]    Specific ceremony years to scrape
  --start-year YEAR          Start of year range
  --end-year YEAR            End of year range

Pipeline options:
  --config FILE              Path to custom settings.yaml
  --force                    Re-scrape even if already checkpointed
  --log-level LEVEL          DEBUG | INFO | WARNING | ERROR (default: INFO)
  --dry-run                  Show what would be scraped without running
  --status                   Show checkpoint status and exit
  --reset-checkpoint         Clear checkpoint (forces full re-run next time)
```

---

## Configuration

All settings live in `config/settings.yaml`. Key sections:

```yaml
scraper:
  start_year: 2000
  end_year: 2023
  request_delay_min: 1.0      # Polite crawl delay (seconds)
  request_delay_max: 3.0
  max_retries: 3

validator:
  completeness_threshold: 0.70  # Warn if <70% of records pass validation

storage:
  sqlite:
    enabled: true
    path: "data/processed/nfa_awards.db"
  excel:
    enabled: true
  csv:
    enabled: true
```

### Environment Variable Overrides

Any config value can be overridden without editing the YAML:

```bash
# Format: NFA__<SECTION>__<KEY>=value
export NFA__SCRAPER__START_YEAR=2010
export NFA__SCRAPER__END_YEAR=2015
python -m nfa_pipeline
```

---

## Output Files

After a successful run, you'll find three files in `data/processed/`:

| File | Format | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `nfa_awards.xlsx` | Excel | Three sheets: Awards, Summary, Invalid Records |
| `nfa_awards.csv` | CSV | UTF-8 with BOM (opens natively in Excel) |
| `nfa_awards.db` | SQLite | Queryable database with full-text indexes |

### Excel Workbook Sheets

**NFA Awards** — main data, one row per award:

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| Year | Ceremony year |
| Film Title | Title as listed in award |
| Language | Primary language of the film |
| Award Category | Full category name |
| Award Type | Golden Lotus / Silver Lotus / Certificate of Merit |
| Director | Credited director(s) |
| Awardee | Person(s) who received the award |
| … | and more |

**Summary** — yearly breakdown of award counts and languages.

**Invalid Records** — records that failed validation, with error messages.

---

## Data Model

```python
class AwardRecord(BaseModel):
    ceremony_year: int           # e.g. 2023
    ceremony_number: int | None  # e.g. 70 (70th NFA)
    category: str                # "Best Film — Golden Lotus"
    category_normalized: str     # "best-film-golden-lotus"
    film_title: str              # "Kantara"
    film_language: str | None    # "Kannada"
    film_year: int | None        # 2022
    director: str | None         # "Rishab Shetty"
    awardee: str | None          # Person who accepted the award
    production_company: str | None
    award_type: str | None       # "Golden Lotus" | "Silver Lotus" | "Certificate of Merit"
    source_url: str | None
    is_valid: bool
    validation_errors: list[str]
    validation_warnings: list[str]
```

